<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Dawn Meats bids for Sims meat business-paper.</title>
<headline>Dawn Meats bids for Sims meat business-paper.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dawn Meats, which accounts for around 15 percent of the Irish national beef kill, has made a bid for the meat business of the publicly-quoted Sims Food Group Plc in the UK, the Irish Independent reported on Friday.</p>
<p>The cost of the acquisition should be around 15 million Irish pounds, depending on the due diligence process now underway, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Sims has two slaughtering operations in Bedford and Hull and six centralised packing plants which handle beef, lamb, pork and venison.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
